{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"AWS Elemental MediaConnect Router now supports configurable recovery latency modes - AWS","context":"AWS Elemental MediaConnect Router has introduced configurable latency settings, allowing users to control the internal connection latency between inputs and outputs. Previously, the latency inside the router was set automatically and couldn't be adjusted. The router now offers two latency configuration options on router outputs: balanced mode and low-latency mode. Balanced mode maintains the existing behavior for general use cases, while low-latency mode optimizes the internal connection recovery time for latency-sensitive workflows. The latency setting can be configured and viewed using the MediaConnect API, AWS Management Console, or AWS CLI. This feature is available in all regions where MediaConnect Router is deployed. A new CloudWatch metric, RouteFabricRecoveryLatency, provides visibility into the configured recovery latency for each route","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/08/mediaconnect-router-latency-modes/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"aws-network-monitoring","skill_description":"Installs, configures, and troubleshoots Network Flow Monitor agents on EC2 instances to monitor network path health. Covers agent installation, IAM permissions, monitoring network paths, and troubleshooting agents reporting no metrics, HTTP 403 errors, or connectivity failures.\n\nServices: network-flow-monitor, ec2, ssm, cloudwatch\nTasks: deploy, debug\nPersona: developer, devops, network-engineer\nWorkload: networking\n*","skill_name":"aws-network-monitoring"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"troubleshooting-application-failures","skill_description":"Troubleshoots failing applications by discovering and analyzing CloudWatch log groups to identify error patterns, root causes, and actionable solutions. Use when an application is experiencing failures and log-based diagnosis is needed.\n\nServices: cloudwatch, lambda, api-gateway, ecs\nTasks: troubleshoot, debug, monitor\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: monitoring\n*","skill_name":"troubleshooting-application-failures"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"aws-media-services","skill_description":"Designs, deploys, reviews, evaluates, audits, and troubleshoots video streaming workflows across AWS media services (MediaConnect, MediaLive, MediaConvert, MediaPackage v2, MediaTailor, CloudFront). Includes per-service validation rules, cross-service workflow patterns for live streaming, linear channels, VOD pipelines, and live-to-VOD, service-specific troubleshooting, best practices assessment, cost optimization, encoder settings, DRM, SCTE-35 ad insertion, epoch locking, and CDN cache configuration.\n\nServices: mediaconnect, medialive, mediaconvert, mediapackage, mediatailor, cloudfront\nTasks: review, deploy, troubleshoot, audit, optimize\nPersona: video-engineer, solutions-architect\nWorkload: live-streaming, vod, linear-channel","skill_name":"aws-media-services"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Search AWS docs for MediaConnect flow monitoring viewer-impacting packet loss metric", "parent_id": "aa0eac2f-cb89-4cf4-9ad2-21878af301eb"}
